        },
        "reason-4": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "number": "4",
            "title": "\"BPA-free\" was never the same as \"plastic-free\"",
            "body": "<p>The baby bottle industry leaned hard on the marketing term \"BPA-free\" because it sounds like safety. It isn't the same thing. <strong>BPA-free only means one specific chemical, Bisphenol-A, is absent.</strong> It says nothing about the plastic physically shedding microparticles when heated. A federal judge made the difference obvious in 2025, ruling that a <strong>\"BPA-free\" label only promises the absence of BPA, not freedom from microplastics</strong>. The big brands were selling false reassurance to hopeful parents, leaving their material quality untouched.</p>"
          }
        },
        "image-5": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image": "https://mokababy.co/cdn/shop/t/12/assets/moka-listicle-plastic-contact-diagram-4x3.jpg?v=135430520556431362981783477680",
            "alt": "Polypropylene contact parts in common glass baby bottle designs",
            "caption": "Comparison showing polypropylene parts that contact hot milk in common glass bottle designs"
          }
        },
        "reason-5": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "number": "5",
            "title": "Even most \"glass\" bottles still put polypropylene against your baby's milk",
            "body": "<p>Switching to glass feels like the fix until you look closer at the big brands. Dr. Brown's, Philips Avent and Comotomo use a real glass body, but <strong>the collar, vent and parts that meet hot milk are often still polypropylene</strong>, the exact plastic from the study. Philips Avent and Dr. Brown's are now facing <strong>class-action lawsuits filed in 2024</strong>, alleging they failed to warn parents that their polypropylene bottles release microplastics when heated. Nuk and Tommee Tippee face similar claims. \"Glass\" on the label can still mean plastic where it counts.</p>"
          }
        },
        "image-6": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image": "https://mokababy.co/cdn/shop/t/12/assets/moka-listicle-lab-testing-4x3.jpg?v=37321869051312854511783477676",
            "alt": "Moka bottle components being measured during product testing",
            "caption": "Moka bottle and nipple components being measured during product testing"
