        "reason-7": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "number": "7",
            "title": "What touches the milk is borosilicate glass and medical-grade silicone, not polypropylene",
            "body": "<p>This is the whole point. Moka's milk-contact surfaces are <strong>borosilicate glass and medical-grade silicone</strong>, the two materials independent testing consistently ranks safest under heat. The structural hard parts use PPSU, engineered to survive repeated sterilization at temperatures that would degrade ordinary polypropylene, so it isn't subject to the same heat-driven breakdown that sheds microplastics. <strong>Every batch is third-party lab-tested and verified.</strong> You're paying for the materials the cheaper bottles skip.</p>"
          }
        },
